+# Local guest Assistant image
+
+This build adds a separate guest chat path inside the board Assistant widget. Signed-in users retain the upstream Assistant.
+
+Set `HOMARR_GUEST_ASSISTANT=true` on Homarr to opt in. Guest chat requires a public board with an Assistant placement and an enabled **custom OpenAI-compatible** provider in Management → Assistant. API keys and headers stay server-side. Public users get text chat only, without Homarr tools, attachments, model selection or service access.
+
+Conversation text is kept in this browser tab's session storage, not in Homarr's conversation tables. New chat clears it. Each request sends up to 20 text messages (2,000 characters per message and 32 KiB total), returns up to 1,024 output tokens, and times out after 90 seconds. Per application process, limits are 10 requests/minute per visitor and trusted network identity, 60/minute total, and 4 active streams. Visitors behind the same proxy identity share the network budget.
+
+Disabling the environment variable, making the board private, or removing its Assistant widget disables the guest route. Admin APIs still require authentication. Existing logged-in cookies are never issued or reused for guests.
+
+The deployment source is based on upstream commit `ebbe134c5e9fa3400266fc8c0199ff54e903634b`. To update upstream, rebase and re-run the focused tests, typecheck, image build and logged-out checks before replacing the deployed image.
