+# Guest Assistant implementation
+
+Goal: opt-in anonymous chat on public boards with an Assistant placement, using the configured custom OpenAI-compatible provider. Signed-in Assistant remains unchanged.
+
+1. Test authorization policy, cookie tampering, bounded messages and request limits.
+2. Add a separate guest route: verify public board and placement on every request, same-origin POST, signed HttpOnly visitor cookie, bounded body/history/output, per-visitor/IP/global budgets and bounded concurrency. No tools, integrations, attachments, model selection or database conversation storage.
+3. Render a guest conversation surface inside the native Assistant widget when logged out. History belongs to the browser tab, not an authenticated user. Support streaming, cancellation, clear history and accessible controls.
+4. Build from the deployed upstream commit, run focused checks, and test on a temporary loopback port with a copied database.
+5. Back up active configuration/data, deploy the custom image in the existing Compose project with HOMARR_GUEST_ASSISTANT=true, and verify logged-out chat, private-board denial and unchanged protected management APIs. Preserve rollback image/config.
+
+Guest mode intentionally supports only the currently configured custom provider. Limits are per application process. Admin keys never enter the browser. Do not change Caddy.
